1
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:06,077
(Sheldon:)And here's another
interesting weather fact.

2
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:08,740
Another? Great!

3
00:00:08,909 --> 00:00:12,019
(Sheldon:)Changes in jet streams
can affect the speed

4
00:00:12,179 --> 00:00:14,419
(Sheldon:)at which the Earth
rotates on its axis,

5
00:00:14,581 --> 00:00:17,931
(Sheldon:)so bad weather can actually
make the day longer.

6
00:00:18,085 --> 00:00:21,555
(Penny:)Well, there must be a hell
of a storm somewhere.

7
00:00:22,656 --> 00:00:26,666
(Sheldon:)Joke if you must, but you're
going to miss these moments.

8
00:00:26,827 --> 00:00:28,537
(Sheldon:)With Leonard home in a few days,

9
00:00:28,695 --> 00:00:31,535
(Sheldon:)this was your last time
driving me to the grocery store.

10
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,838
(Penny:)You know, I will miss this.

11
00:00:34,001 --> 00:00:36,541
(Sheldon:)I'll tell you what,
if my apples are mealy,

12
00:00:36,703 --> 00:00:41,213
(Sheldon:)we'll hit the produce section
for one last crazy blowout.

13
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:43,285
(Sheldon:)Heck, you can even push the cart.

14
00:00:44,444 --> 00:00:47,944
(Sheldon:)Please don't take my looking
forward to Leonard's return

15
00:00:48,115 --> 00:00:51,615
(Sheldon:)as criticism of the job you've
been doing in his absence.

16
00:00:51,785 --> 00:00:53,195
(Penny:)I won't.

17
00:00:53,353 --> 00:00:57,133
(Sheldon:)That criticism will come later
in your report card.

18
00:00:57,291 --> 00:00:59,241
(Penny:)Yeah, I didn't stay
for the detention,

19
00:00:59,393 --> 00:01:01,273
(Penny:)I'm not gonna read
the report card.

20
00:01:05,098 --> 00:01:08,268
(Leonard(in Penny's apartment):)-Hello.
-(SCREAMS) Leonard! Hi!

21
00:01:08,435 --> 00:01:10,035
-Sh! Keep your voice down.
-Oh, my God. You weren't supposed

22
00:01:10,203 --> 00:01:12,153
-to be here till Sunday!
-We finished the experiment early,

23
00:01:12,306 --> 00:01:13,806
sol thought I'd come home
and surprise you.

24
00:01:13,974 --> 00:01:15,214
(Penny:)Oh, my gosh,
why are we whispering?

25
00:01:15,375 --> 00:01:17,945
(Leonard:)I didn't tell Sheldon
so we could have a few days alone.

26
00:01:18,111 --> 00:01:22,491
-Oh! That is so romantic.
-Sure, that's why I did it.

27
00:01:23,984 --> 00:01:25,964
(Penny:)I just cannot believe you're here.

28
00:01:26,119 --> 00:01:27,899
Penny, it's your lucky day!

29
00:01:28,055 --> 00:01:33,025
(Sheldon(off):)Three of the eggs are clearly
not jumbo. Grab your keys.

